      "reasoning": "Jason Wood’s own House speech identifies Ferntree Gully Technical School as a school he attended and says its site was later demolished and replaced by real estate. Victorian government records identify the historical school as No. 7145, renamed Glenfern Secondary College in 1990; in 1997 that school merged with the separate Ferntree Gully Secondary College (No. 7827) to form Ferntree Gully College (No. 7827), which closed in 2006. The 1972 Government Gazette lists the technical school at Main Road, Upper Ferntree Gully. The later No. 7827 college address at Dorset Road and Alma Avenue is not assigned to the former technical school’s campus. The exact recorded historical school is suitable as an individual manual institution; the assertion proposal maps Wood directly to that historical identity and does not map him to the later merged college.",
